# --- Dev/build-only: never shipped to the Render runtime (npm start = app/ws-bridge.js).
# The container only reads app/ + workspace/materials/; everything below is unused at runtime.
#
# Two syntax rules this file lives or dies by (both verified with a real docker build,
# 2026-07-05 — get either wrong and the exclusions silently no-op or nuke the app):
#   1. NO inline/trailing comments. Only a line that STARTS with # is a comment; text
#      after a pattern (e.g. `tools/  # harness`) becomes part of the pattern and matches
#      nothing. Keep each pattern alone on its line.
#   2. Unlike .gitignore, a slash-free pattern matches ONLY at the build-context root,
#      not at any depth. So `materials` excludes the root materials/ mirror but NEVER
#      workspace/materials/. Do NOT rewrite these as recursive `**/materials/` — that
#      WOULD wrongly drop workspace/materials/ and break the app.
#
# What each excludes:
#   tools/     = Playwright harness + 344M gitignored CSS baseline (dev-only)
#   .local/    = gitignored archives / visual audits (dev-only)
#   materials/ = legacy backup mirror; the app reads workspace/materials/
#   .trellis/  = task / planning metadata, not runtime
#   docs/      = docs, not runtime
tools/
.local/
/materials/
.trellis/
docs/
